GAL22V10
UA6RHD13

AB1 AB2 AB3 AB4 AB5 AB6 GALSTB RCFG8 RCFG4 RCFG2 BASEA GND
RW CFGIN NC15 ACPHASE RST DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12 NC22 DRVEN VCC

; =====================================================================
; UA6 - RocHard RH800C  -  ua6_hd + DB13-LOW-DURING-RESET  (RAM bring-up)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; IDENTICAL to ua6_hd.pld (the WORKING HD build, ORIGINAL latched /_DRVEN)
; EXCEPT DB13 (pin 20) is driven LOW while reset is asserted.
;
; WHY (LA-confirmed 2026-08-01):
;   Strap-on red/yellow screen = /_RAMCE fires at $F8 (Kickstart ROM) ->
;   U2 fights the motherboard ROM on D8-15 -> crash. It fires because
;   UA4's /GALCLK1 region-7 term (o19 line37) is ARMED, and that term
;   needs UA4's base latch o16 & o17 & o18 = 1,1,1.
;   LA proved o16.o17.o18 = 1,1,1 at the $F8 fire.
;
;   The crash is the FIRST Kickstart $F8 fetch - BEFORE autoconfig - so
;   the base latch is 111 simply because UA4's self-hold latches
;   (o16=o16, oe=/_DRVEN) SETTLE to 111 at reset-release (bus idle-high).
;   Capturing a base later (ua6_hd_wr write-release) was too late AND
;   destabilised autoconfig -> reverted.
;
; THE FIX UNDER TEST: force o18=0 from RESET.  UA4's oe (=/_DRVEN) is OFF
;   during reset, so UA4 releases /_CFGD13; if UA6 drives DB13 LOW then,
;   /_CFGD13 goes low through R15(32.7R), UA4's o18 feedback tracks 0, and
;   when /_DRVEN asserts at reset-release UA4 holds o18=0 -> line37
;   disarmed -> NO $F8 fire.  DB13 chosen because the controller er_Type
;   ($D1) already has DB13=0, so this does NOT fight the HD identity
;   (forcing DB12 or DB14, which are 1 in $D1, would).
;
;   /_DRVEN is UNCHANGED from ua6_hd (the working latched version), so HD
;   autoconfig should be unaffected.
;
; RISK / NEXT: if o18 drifts back to 1 in the gap between reset-release and
;   the first /_DRVEN assertion, widen DB13.E to also cover "/_DRVEN
;   deasserted" (drive DB13 low the whole oe-off window). Watch CFGD13 on
;   the LA to see if it sticks at 0.
;
; BOARD: game II - DIP-1 ON - DIP-2 ON - JPA1 2M - SIMMs out for 1st check.
; =====================================================================


; ---- /_DRVEN (pin 23) : UNCHANGED, working latched version -----------
/DRVEN = /CFGIN & /BASEA & RST
       + /CFGIN & /DRVEN & RST


; ---- /_AC_PHASE (pin 16) : Hi-Z (unchanged) -------------------------
ACPHASE.T = VCC
ACPHASE.E = AB1 & /AB1


; ---- DB12/14/15 : Hi-Z (unchanged) ----------------------------------
DB15.T = VCC
DB15.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB14.T = VCC
DB14.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB12.T = VCC
DB12.E = AB1 & /AB1

; ---- DB13 (pin 20) : drive LOW while RESET asserted -----------------
; .T = tautological FALSE -> output data = 0 (LOW).  DB13 is active-high
; in the declaration (no slash), so data 0 -> pin LOW.
; .E = /RST -> enabled only while reset asserted (RST pin low); Hi-Z after.
DB13.T = AB1 & /AB1
DB13.E = /RST


; ---- NC15 (pin 15), NC22 (pin 22) : Hi-Z (unchanged) ----------------
NC15.T = VCC
NC15.E = AB1 & /AB1
NC22.T = VCC
NC22.E = AB1 & /AB1


DESCRIPTION

UA6 HD build + DB13-low-during-reset for RocHard RH800C RAM bring-up.

Same as ua6_hd.pld (working HD, latched /_DRVEN, DB/ACPHASE Hi-Z) except
DB13 (pin 20) is driven LOW while reset is asserted. Goal: bias UA4's
o18 (/_CFGD13) base-latch bit to 0 at reset-release so /GALCLK1's region-7
term (needs o16.o17.o18=111) never arms -> /_GALSTROBE / /_RAMCE stop
firing at $F8 (Kickstart), which was the strap-on crash.

TEST (LA, roctec_ram_cfgd channel map):
  1. HD still enumerates / boots with RAM off? (must - /_DRVEN unchanged)
  2. Strap ON: does CFGD13 read 0 (not 1)? does base leave 111?
  3. Strap ON: does /_RAMCE STILL fire at region 1111 ($F8)? Must NOT.
